1
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and let
it fly until it gets there.

3
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:29,340
Walking and talking on
the way back from P.E.,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed,
saying I'm still full of energy as I am.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
Katsushika, tameari.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare, and the unchanging streetscape

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
the sun has already gone down.

11
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:53,900
Do the yakitori vendors really exist?

12
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

13
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:01,700
retiring from people,

14
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,080
the sunset falls.

15
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too, it ends with a drop

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:13,660
Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness is lost.

17
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,300
I realized it, because I'm such a fool.

18
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,740
Laugh and forgive me.

19
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:42,760
Signs of a surge are
showing in the oil market.

20
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:46,100
Buy up related stocks,
a billion dollars' worth each.

21
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:47,180
That's all.

22
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:53,200
President, what would you like for lunch?

23
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:55,100
Sydney in ten minutes, is it?

24
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,640
Right, I'll finish lunch in five minutes.

25
00:01:58,460 --> 00:01:58,960
Get it ready right away.

26
00:01:58,960 --> 00:01:59,680
Yes, sir!

27
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,440
Yes, sir!

28
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:03,810
Eh

29
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:06,420
Eh, it hurts!

30
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:08,280
President, what's wrong?

31
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:08,860
President!

32
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:13,040
President! President! President!

33
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:21,920
What? Nakagawa had emergency surgery?
Is that true?

34
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:25,720
I-it's true, I was eating lunch earlier when

35
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,600
a breaking news bulletin just came in.

36
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:34,700
Keiichi Nakagawa, heir to the Nakagawa Group,
one of the world's leading conglomerates,

37
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,540
in the early hours of today, Japan time,

38
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:41,240
apparently suffered abdominal pain aboard his private
plane while in transit and underwent emergency surgery.

39
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:43,720
Nakagawa?

40
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,080
That's what happened.

41
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:49,500
It's on the internet too.

42
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:52,200
It's being broadcast all over the world.

43
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:57,240
That's terrible!
Let's go to the hospital right away.

44
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,200
So this is the hospital.

45
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:12,100
It's supposed to be a Nakagawa Group hospital,
apparently.

46
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:13,060
Yoo-hoo!

47
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:19,220
Yoo-hoo!

48
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,520
Hahaha!

49
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:28,580
Excuse me,
is this Nakagawa International Hospital?

50
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:30,160
That's right.

51
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:34,620
A man named Keiichi Nakagawa
should be hospitalized here, though.

52
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:38,840
President Keiichi who was hospitalized
for acute appendicitis, right?

53
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,560
Acute appendicitis.

54
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,800
Just appendicitis.

55
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,700
It's just appendicitis?

56
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:46,920
It wasn't worth all of us coming to visit

57
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:50,660
But since we came all this way,
let's at least see Kei-chan's face.

58
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:52,520
So, what room is he in?

59
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:56,360
He's on the top floor of that building.

60
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:00,340
So this really is the hospital.

61
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,880
Dr. Mahi Mahi.

62
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,380
It's almost time for surgery.

63
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,400
Yo. I'll bring the longboard.

64
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:11,000
Here, this.

65
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:13,840
Jarei!

66
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:15,620
Aloha!

67
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:19,200
That person just now
must have been the doctor.

68
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,340
What kind of hospital is this?

69
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:23,340
Anyway, let's go in.

70
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:36,860
Thank you for waiting.

71
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:40,060
Visitation for Keiichi
Nakagawa has been approved.

72
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,300
Well, this is the entrance.

73
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:45,160
What is this place?

74
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:49,880
It's a waterway. Please proceed by boat.

75
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:59,060
Sorry to keep you waiting. We didn't come here to play,
we want to see Nakagawa. We understand that.

76
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:07,140
The elevator to the special ward is deep in the jungle.
It's like walking on solid ground, isn't it?

77
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:10,000
Feels like we're going somewhere, right?

78
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:14,340
Ahhhh, has everyone boarded?!

79
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:23,000
Welcome aboard the Jungle Boat! I'm your captain, Donald Cook.
Save the applause and just get going already!

80
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:27,260
You're a tough crowd, aren't you?
Alright, let's set sail!

81
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:38,520
Looks like we've finally arrived.

82
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:39,740
Yeah, we have.

83
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,200
Now, behind that door...

84
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,060
Wrong one! It was Elephant-san's apartment!

85
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,940
Now Jaws is attacking us!

86
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:56,520
Why is there a shark in the jungle!

87
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:03,320
We're done for! Now it's Backdraft!

88
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:05,220
What kind of attraction is this!

89
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:08,340
Just hurry up and take us to Nakagawa!

90
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:12,400
Understood.
You're a tough crowd to please, though.

91
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:17,700
The special ward is at
the back of this temple.

92
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:21,360
This temple looks like a
movie we've seen somewhere.

93
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,640
Where are we, anyway?

94
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,000
It's a hospital.

95
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,560
Are we really going to get there?

96
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:38,440
There it is, over there!

97
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,540
Please, come in.

98
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:44,560
So you're finally here.

99
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:46,460
Thanks.

100
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:49,960
You look healthier than I expected.

101
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:52,440
Doctor, how is his progress?

102
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:56,540
He's recovering well after surgery.
He can be discharged in a week.

103
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:59,720
Thank goodness. I was so worried.

104
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:02,300
Sorry we couldn't get in touch.

105
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:04,680
It's just appendicitis,
you're making a big fuss.

106
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:08,880
Are you all right, Kei-chan?

107
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:11,140
That's where he had the surgery, though.

108
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,080
Was it? Sorry, sorry.

109
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,420
Where should we put the flowers?

110
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,320
Right. Then let's move the TV.

111
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,120
Heave-ho, shot!

112
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:32,436
Shot,

113
00:07:32,486 --> 00:07:42,380
Shot.

114
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:45,260
Nakagawa,
does it hurt that much when you laugh?

115
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,000
Listen, Nishino Ryoji.

116
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,031
Sorry, sorry.

117
00:07:55,081 --> 00:07:57,460
So it was true after all.

118
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:58,621
By the way, Nakagawa,

119
00:07:58,671 --> 00:08:02,480
