an amusement park attraction?

120
00:08:03,528 --> 00:08:07,260
I wanted to brighten up
the image of the hospital.

121
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,420
I see.

122
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:12,720
But once you're a patient, you're stuck
in your room, so you can't really tell.

123
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:15,080
So you only figured that out once
you were hospitalized yourself?

124
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:18,280
Idiot, let's just head back already.

125
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:22,060
We can manage. Sorry, sorry.

126
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:23,740
Honestly, you're something else.

127
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:27,500
If we stay too long,
who knows what Ryotsu will do.

128
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:30,260
He seems fine, so shall we head out soon?

129
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:32,040
That would be better, I think.

130
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:34,860
Well then, Nakagawa, take care.

131
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:36,020
Thank you very much.

132
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:36,780
Thank you very much.

133
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:40,880
Well then,

134
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:41,180
Well then,

135
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,740
Hey,

136
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,420
You idiot!

137
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:50,120
Ryo-chan, really.

138
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:52,380
We came all this way to visit him,

139
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:58,780
but Mr. Nakagawa, who was hospitalized
at Nakagawa International Hospital,

140
00:08:58,780 --> 00:09:00,680
was discharged safely yesterday.

141
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:02,360
It was only appendicitis.

142
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:04,260
Even his discharge made the news.

143
00:09:04,260 --> 00:09:07,740
It was broadcast worldwide on CNN, too.

144
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:10,740
At this rate, if Nakagawa so much as trips,
it'll be a huge deal.

145
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:14,040
If he so much as farts,
the whole world will panic!

146
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:20,380
Yes, once Kei-chan's fart sent
the world economy into chaos.

147
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:22,400
Did that really happen?

148
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:27,640
When Kei-chan was hospitalized this time, apparently
Japan's stock prices dropped quite a bit too.

149
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:29,040
No way!

150
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:41,080
Congratulations on your discharge,
Nakagawa-san.

151
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:42,260
Thank you.

152
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:47,960
You're really popular, aren't you?

153
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:50,340
Even on TV shows, the impact has been huge.

154
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:55,460
If I'm hospitalized, do you think it
would have much of an effect on the public?

155
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:57,540
In your case, probably

156
00:09:58,380 --> 00:09:59,760
Have you decided on lunch?

157
00:09:59,920 --> 00:10:01,340
I guess it's udon after all.

158
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:02,940
Yeah, udon's fine.

159
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:06,780
Trouble! Senpai has been hospitalized!

160
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:26,900


161
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:29,100
Nakagawa, this isn't the place to laugh!

162
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:31,300
Sorry.

163
00:10:32,220 --> 00:10:34,360
Chief, don't make me laugh.

164
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:36,980
It still hurts my wound when I laugh.

165
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:38,980
Sorry, sorry.

166
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,900
You're the only one crying for me.

167
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:44,520
My bosom friend!

168
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:48,540
The Chief went too far,
and Keichan laughed too much.

169
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:54,000
We're the same humans,
so why is the treatment so different?

170
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,960
It's really frustrating.

171
00:10:57,400 --> 00:11:00,380
Senpai, all humans are equal.

172
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,240
Rather than a number one like me,

173
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:06,420
someone like you someone like you,

174
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:09,540
the only-one type is the one to envy.

175
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:11,940
Just helping is pitiful.

176
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:15,520
Hey, don't say that with
such a refreshing smile.

177
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:19,160
You're talking from a high position,
aren't you?

178
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:22,740
Doesn't "only one" just mean
"and various others"?

179
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:25,780
Higher position?

180
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:27,440
At a higher position!

181
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:31,780
That's cruel, senpai's down at
such a low position, it's pitiful!

182
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:32,960
That only makes it worse, you know!

183
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:34,909
That was one word too many.

184
00:11:34,959 --> 00:11:37,640
Ryo-chan, you've really gotten twisted.

185
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:39,900
He's a small-minded man, after all.

186
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:44,294
Damn. Trying to fix the mood
of a senpai in this state,

187
00:11:44,344 --> 00:11:46,880
is harder than rebuilding Japan's economy.

188
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,054
No, s-, s-, senpai is

189
00:11:50,104 --> 00:11:52,940
the only one of the only ones.

190
00:11:55,100 --> 00:12:00,700
Senpai's face is unique, and his behavior
goes beyond being a police officer,

191
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:03,860
Nakagawa, your face is twitching!

192
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:07,200
When it comes to getting laughs,
he's the best in the world.

193
00:12:07,820 --> 00:12:12,080
Right, senpai is also
number one in that sense.

194
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:15,640
Kei-chan, that's not helping at all.

195
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,680
That's enough, Ryo-chan.

196
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:21,380
Yeah.

197
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:24,900
That was just a joke.

198
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:27,880
Did that surprise you?
Hey, were you surprised?

199
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:30,300
Please stop it already, senpai.

200
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:33,420
The senpai isn't the type to get
upset over something like this,

201
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,360
so I thought something was off.

202
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:37,340
It was just a little prank.

203
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:40,280
Then you didn't have to hit so hard.

204
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:41,860
Sorry about that.

205
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:46,179
The world's number one laughingstock

206
00:12:46,229 --> 00:12:47,540
Nakagawa, you...

207
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:50,320
If it's come to this, I'll make them
laugh until they're completely wrecked,

208
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:52,960
I'll give them stomachaches!

209
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:12,600
My friend Bae Yong-joon

210
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:14,200
Doesn't look like him at all.

211
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:17,300
Speaking of Bae,

212
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,760
Is this the one?

213
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:22,000
Hato-chan Pii

214
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:23,880
Is that too old?

215
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:30,280
Kristic committee member, I'm the parent.

216
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:33,600
Well, this one does look
a bit like him, yeah.

217
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:53,080
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa

218
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:54,780
Anyway, the lottery's already spinning.

219
00:13:54,780 --> 00:13:56,060
What? Oh shit.

220
00:13:57,780 --> 00:13:59,360
Who's that?

221
00:14:00,730 --> 00:14:01,700
It's Ayaya.

222
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:06,660
Ayaya

223
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:12,800
You got fooled by Ayaya, didn't you?

224
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,640
Looks like you like it

225
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:06,580
You put soba dipping sauce in a cola bottle?

226
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:08,620
It's the same as making a mistake.

227
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:12,820
Why would you put soba
sauce in a cola bottle?

228
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,800
I've never done that either.

229
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:15,760
Fine, fine.

230
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:17,660
This is why the super-rich are like this.

231
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:19,420
Well, never mind.

232
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:22,860
Anyway,
I was going to have Korira-kun drink it.

233
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:25,400
Hey, you're trying to
experiment on me again!

234
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:27,340
What kind of new medicine is it, anyway?

235
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:28,760
The medicine I took...

236
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:31,420
Well, its effects should
kick in any moment now.

237
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:33,580
The principal is...

238
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:34,940
in top form.

239
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:41,480
It's such a lame gag, so why is it so funny?

240
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:43,540
Looks like it's a big hit. Well then, next.

241
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:46,560
Itamai-san, there you are, Itamai!

242
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:49,720
My stomach hurts!

243
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:51,680
It does seem the drug has an effect.

244
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:53,840
So laughing is the effect

245
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:57,040
Hey, Professor, what drug is this?

246
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:59,480
He's laughing while he's angry!

247
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:01,761
Shut up! My feelings are angry, but

248
00:16:01,811 --> 00:16:03,560
